## 5. SECURITY RULES

Never:

* trust client-side authorization
* allow cross-tenant access
* store secrets in source control
* expose passwords/tokens/API keys
* use unrestricted file uploads
* allow unrestricted LLM database writes
* silently modify posted financial records
* create duplicate financial transactions
* bypass approval requirements
* fake GST filing success
* scrape government portals without appropriate approval/legal review

Use:

* secure authentication
* short-lived access tokens
* refresh rotation/revocation
* secure cookies/BFF where appropriate
* MFA
* Argon2id
* rate limiting
* brute-force protection
* RBAC
* tenant guards
* object-level authorization
* MIME validation
* malware scanning
* private object storage
* signed URLs
* encryption
* audit logs
* request IDs
* secret/PII redaction
* dependency scanning
* container scanning
* secret scanning
* backup and restore testing

## 6. FINANCIAL DATA RULES

Financial correctness has priority over convenience.

Enforce:

* debit = credit
* deterministic calculations
* decimal-safe monetary values
* idempotent financial writes
* transactional posting
* immutable/append-oriented posted records
* reversal/correction instead of silent mutation
* financial-period locking
* safe invoice numbering
* audit event for critical mutations
* tenant/business boundaries

Never allow AI output to become accounting truth without deterministic validation and the configured approval policy.

## 7. AI/OCR RULES

AI is an assistant, not the accounting authority.

Every extracted field should support:

* value
* normalized value
* confidence
* source
* model/provider
* model version
* document/page location where available
* verification state
* reviewer
* verification timestamp

AI processing must use structured output and schema validation.

Accounting calculations must be deterministic.

AI actions must be auditable.

